  {
    "subject": "vectors",
    "question": "How do I add two vectors?",
    "firstWordsMs": 2943,
    "speech": [
      "Let's see exactly how that works by drawing the vectors.\n",
      "To add two vectors graphically, use the tip-to-tail method. You place the tail of the second vector right at the tip of the first vector, keeping both of their directions and lengths intact. The sum, or resultant vector, goes straight from the tail of the first vector to the tip of the second vector.\n\nIf you are working with coordinate numbers, you simply add their corresponding components together: add the horizontal x-values to get the new x, and add the vertical y-values to get the new y. Does that make sense?"
